      "facts": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "S1",
          "en": "The `@request_method` variable is initialized with the result of `check_method(super)`. This supports the fact that the `request_method` is determined by the original request method, which may be overridden by the `rack.methodoverride.original_method` header.",
          "pt-br": "A vari\u00e1vel `@request_method` \u00e9 inicializada com o resultado de `check_method(super)`. Isso suporta a fato de que o m\u00e9todo de solicita\u00e7\u00e3o \u00e9 determinado pelo m\u00e9todo original de solicita\u00e7\u00e3o, que pode ser sobrescrito pelo cabe\u00e7alho `rack.methodoverride.original_method`."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "S2",
          "en": "The `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[request_method]` expression returns the HTTP method corresponding to the `request_method` variable. This supports the fact that the HTTP method is determined by the `request_method` variable.",
          "pt-br": "A express\u00e3o `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[method]` retorna o m\u00e9todo HTTP correspondente \u00e0 vari\u00e1vel `method`."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "S3",
          "en": "The `@method` variable is initialized with the result of `check_method` if the `args` array is empty, otherwise it falls back to the original `super` method. This supports the fact that the `method` is determined by the original request method or the `rack.methodoverride.original_method` header if no `args` array is provided.",
          "pt-br": "A vari\u00e1vel `@method` \u00e9 inicializada com o resultado de `check_method` se o array `args` estiver vazio, caso contr\u00e1rio ela recai para o m\u00e9todo original `super`."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "S4",
          "en": "The `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[method]` expression returns the HTTP method corresponding to the `method` variable. This supports the fact that the HTTP method is determined by the `method` variable.",
          "pt-br": "A express\u00e3o `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[method]` retorna o m\u00e9todo HTTP correspondente \u00e0 vari\u00e1vel `method`."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "S4",
          "en": "The `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[method]` expression returns the HTTP method corresponding to the `method` variable. This supports the fact that the HTTP method is determined by the `method` variable.",
          "pt-br": "A express\u00e3o `HTTP_METHOD_LOOKUP[method]` retorna o m\u00e9todo HTTP correspondente \u00e0 vari\u00e1vel `method`."
        }
      ],
